        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3191bc05-c9e4-5a7b-a4b4-02ca877b61ee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jaroslav Kvapil, Antonín Dvořák\n- Places: Chudenice, Prague, Kingdom of Bohemia, Central Europe, Czech Republic\n- Works: Rusalka\n- Concepts: Czech literature, opera, monarchy\n\nFacts:\n- Jaroslav Kvapil was born on 25 September 1868 in Chudenice in the Kingdom of Bohemia.\n- The Kingdom of Bohemia was a medieval and early modern monarchy in Central Europe.\n- The Kingdom of Bohemia was the predecessor of the modern Czech Republic.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil was a Czech poet, playwright, and librettist.\n- Rusalka is an opera described as a lyric fairy tale by Antonín Dvořák.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil died on 10 January 1950 in Prague.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a07e2f9e-de9c-5df2-b06f-ac0658183274",
        "text": "Page: Jaroslav Kvapil. Sentence: Jaroslav Kvapil (25 September 1868 in Chudenice, Kingdom of Bohemia – 10 January 1950 in Prague) was a Czech poet, playwright, and librettist.\nPage: Kingdom of Bohemia. Sentence: The Kingdom of Bohemia, sometimes in English literature referred to as the Czech Kingdom (Czech: \"České království\" ; German: \"Königreich Böhmen\" ; Latin: \"Regnum Bohemiae\" , sometimes Latin: \"Regnum Czechorum\" ), was a medieval and early modern monarchy in Central Europe, the predecessor of the modern Czech Republic.\nPage: Rusalka (opera). Sentence: 114, is an opera ('lyric fairy tale') by Antonín Dvořák.",
